From 8ac11133428f8bcb56406253c131047819b61171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Gamb <nick.gamb@solo.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:02:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(workerpool): pod identity for worker pods
 (serviceAccountName, labels, annotations)

An actor's traffic leaves through its worker pod, so the worker pod's
ServiceAccount is the workload identity every call the actor makes carries
(for example a service mesh's SPIFFE ID, or cloud workload identity). Today
every worker runs as the namespace's default ServiceAccount and a pool can't
say otherwise, nor can it annotate its pods for the CNI or mesh.

WorkerPoolPodTemplate gains:

- serviceAccountName: the ServiceAccount the worker pods run as.
- labels: added to the worker pods. ate.dev/worker-pool stays owned by the
  pool (CEL: reserved), and the controller always stamps it.
- annotations: added to the worker pods, e.g. to tell a mesh how to treat
  the actor's veth (Istio: istio.io/reroute-virtual-interfaces: ateom0).

The Deployment is still server-side applied, so removing a field from the
pool removes it from the pods.
